<!--
  This covers the site's fixed, static pages only. Dynamic content
  (individual articles, players, teams, leagues, quizzes, wallpapers)
  lives in Firestore and can't be enumerated in a static file - that
  needs a small build-time or scheduled script that queries Firestore
  and regenerates this file, which is a good candidate to fold into
  the same automation job discussed for live stats. Until then,
  search engines will still discover dynamic pages by following links
  from these static pages and from each other.
-->
